                <pb facs="0777" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90G2/37: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-03T13:00:00+03:00">December 3, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 3—9:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>50. The Minister for Foreign Affairs Towfiq Suwaidi and I signed the Treaty of
                    Commerce and Navigation at noon today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For text of treaty, see Department of State Treaty Series No. 960, or 54
                        Stat. 1790.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
